17. Check if a number is even or odd and print it out. Use switch case to solve the problem:

import java.util.*;
public class Main {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        Scanner sc = new Scanner(System.in);
        int a = sc.nextInt();
        switch (a % 2) {
            case 0:
                System.out.println("EVEN");
                break;
            case 1:
                System.out.println("ODD");
                break;
            default:
                System.out.println("Unexpected input");
        }
    }
}
